{{!-- The Authors Directory: the masthead. A Surface that lists people, not posts.

Its sibling Surface, the author archive at /author/{slug}/, lists one writer's posts — see
author.hbs. Shared by page-authors.hbs and custom-authors.hbs so no markup is duplicated.

A MASTHEAD LISTS PEOPLE WHO HAVE WRITTEN. Every staff account is an "author" to Ghost, so an owner
or an editor who has not published yet would render as a row reading "No posts" — on this install
that was a sixth writer beside the design's five.

The guard is in the loop rather than in the query because `count.posts` is NOT filterable on
authors in Ghost 6: `filter="count.posts:>0"`, `":>=1"` and `":-0"` each return an empty set
rather than a filtered one. Ordering by `count.posts desc` means the first row carries the highest
count, so testing that one row is enough to know whether anybody has published at all — without
the outer check, a publication with no posts renders an empty bordered list.

That ordering is also the design's: the masthead runs from the most prolific writer down, unlike
the Tags Directory, which is alphabetical because a subject list is browsed rather than ranked.

`limit="100"` is declared rather than `"all"` because Ghost 6 caps every {{#get}} at 100 silently
(core/shared/max-limit-cap.js). --}}
{{#post}}
	{{> "page-intro" eyebrow=(t "The masthead") headingId="au-title"}}

	{{#get "authors" include="count.posts" order="count.posts desc" limit="100" as |authors|}}
		{{#if authors.[0].count.posts}}
			{{#match @custom.directory_layout "Cover cards"}}
				{{> "directory/author-cards" authors=authors}}
			{{else}}
				{{> "directory/author-rows" authors=authors}}
			{{/match}}
		{{else}}
			<section class="container pt-16">
				<p class="font-body text-muted">{{t "No writers yet."}}</p>
			</section>
		{{/if}}
	{{/get}}

	{{> "newsletter" anchor="authors-newsletter" pt="pt-20"}}
{{/post}}
